"path":232,"stem":233,"icon":234},"CRI Format","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fcri-format","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F01.cri-format","i-lucide-link",{"title":236,"path":237,"stem":238,"icon":239},"Grind Jobs","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fgrind-jobs","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F02.grind-jobs","i-lucide-workflow",{"title":241,"path":242,"stem":243,"icon":178},"Project Publishing Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fproject-publishing-design","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F03.project-publishing-design",{"title":245,"path":246,"stem":247,"icon":33},"Sign-In Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fsign-in-design","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F04.sign-in-design",{"title":249,"path":250,"stem":251,"icon":252},"Development Server","\u002Fplatform\u002Fdevelopment-server","04.platform\u002F13.development-server","i-lucide-server-cog",{"title":254,"path":255,"stem":256,"icon":257},"Supply Chain Security","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsupply-chain-security","04.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security","i-lucide-package-check",{"title":259,"path":260,"stem":261,"icon":262},"Enterprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","04.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":264,"title":231,"body":265,"description":1237,"extension":1238,"links":1239,"meta":1240,"navigation":1241,"path":232,"seo":1242,"stem":233,"__hash__":1243},"docs\u002F04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F01.cri-format.md",{"type":266,"value":267,"toc":1220},"minimark",[268,272,276,280,291,298,302,312,318,322,327,330,369,373,380,387,393,397,404,459,465,475,488,552,555,623,626,630,633,639,643,646,652,656,659,665,669,676,916,920,926,1127,1131,1216],[269,270,26],"h2",{"id":271},"overview",[273,274,275],"p",{},"A CRI (Kinotic Resource Identifier) is used by Kinotic to route requests to the appropriate service, method, or event stream. It is a URI-like format with parts named for clarity within the Kinotic platform.",[269,277,279],{"id":278},"format","Format",[281,282,287],"pre",{"className":283,"code":285,"language":286},[284],"language-text","scheme:\u002F\u002F[scope@][zone~]resourceName[\u002Fpath][#version]\n","text",[288,289,285],"code",{"__ignoreMap":290},"",[273,292,293,294,297],{},"Everything in brackets (",[288,295,296],{},"[]",") is optional.",[269,299,301],{"id":300},"case","Case",[273,303,304,305,308,309,311],{},"Every part keeps the case it was written with, and addresses match by exact string comparison — ",[288,306,307],{},"OrderService"," and ",[288,310,307],{}," are two different addresses. Service names carry the case of the class that published them, so a typical address looks like:",[281,313,316],{"className":314,"code":315,"language":286},[284],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~org.kinotic.management.api.services.ProjectService\u002FfindByRepoFullName\n",[288,317,315],{"__ignoreMap":290},[269,319,321],{"id":320},"components","Components",[323,324,326],"h3",{"id":325},"scheme","Scheme",[273,328,329],{},"Identifies the type of resource being addressed.",[331,332,333,345],"table",{},[334,335,336],"thead",{},[337,338,339,342],"tr",{},[340,341,326],"th",{},[340,343,344],{},"Description",[346,347,348,359],"tbody",{},[337,349,350,356],{},[351,352,353],"td",{},[288,354,355],{},"srv",[351,357,358],{},"Published services and their methods",[337,360,361,366],{},[351,362,363],{},[288,364,365],{},"stream",[351,367,368],{},"Event streams (not yet routable through the gateway)",[323,370,372],{"id":371},"scope","Scope",[273,374,375,376,379],{},"An optional qualifier that narrows the CRI to a specific context, such as a tenant ID, user ID, or device ID. When present, it appears before the ",[288,377,378],{},"@"," symbol.",[273,381,382,383,386],{},"If a scope needs sub-scopes, use the format ",[288,384,385],{},"scope:sub-scope",".",[281,388,391],{"className":389,"code":390,"language":286},[284],"srv:\u002F\u002Ftenant-123@app.acme-org.orders-app~OrderService\nstream:\u002F\u002Fdevice-42@app.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\u002Fsensor-1\n",[288,392,390],{"__ignoreMap":290},[323,394,396],{"id":395},"zone","Zone",[273,398,399,400,403],{},"The optional zone places the resource in the isolation boundary the gateway validates on every send and subscribe. It precedes the resourceName, separated by ",[288,401,402],{},"~",". A zone is one or more dot-separated labels of lowercase letters, digits, and interior dashes.",[331,405,406,414],{},[334,407,408],{},[337,409,410,412],{},[340,411,396],{},[340,413,344],{},[346,415,416,429,439,449],{},[337,417,418,423],{},[351,419,420],{},[288,421,422],{},"app.\u003CorganizationId>.\u003CapplicationId>",[351,424,425,426,386],{},"One application's services. Only that application's participants and the owning organization's runtimes can call them, through the app server, the one server that reaches these zones; they are hosted by the owning organization's runtime, which authenticates as an organization participant. Applications may nest their own sub-zones, e.g. ",[288,427,428],{},"app.acme-org.orders-app.billing",[337,430,431,436],{},[351,432,433],{},[288,434,435],{},"app-api",[351,437,438],{},"The platform's data plane for applications, such as entity persistence and named query execution. Hosted in-process by the platform only.",[337,440,441,446],{},[351,442,443],{},[288,444,445],{},"management-api",[351,447,448],{},"The platform services organizations manage the system through, such as member, application, and entity definition management. Hosted in-process by the platform only.",[337,450,451,456],{},[351,452,453],{},[288,454,455],{},"system-api",[351,457,458],{},"The system's own services. Only system participants can call or host them.",[273,460,461,462,464],{},"A cluster member outside the platform's servers can host its services in ",[288,463,445],{},", where organizations' users call them through the management server as they call the platform's own; such a service checks the caller's organization itself.",[273,466,467,468,471,472,474],{},"Organization and application ids become zone labels, but only ever after the ",[288,469,470],{},"app"," prefix, so they cannot collide with the platform's own zones. The one exception is guarded explicitly: creating an organization or application whose name slugifies to ",[288,473,455],{}," is rejected.",[273,476,477,478,480,481,484,485,487],{},"Which zones a connection may address is determined by the authenticated participant. A participant may also address any sub-zone of a zone it is allowed, so ",[288,479,428],{}," is reachable by whoever may reach ",[288,482,483],{},"app.acme-org.orders-app",". An address without a ",[288,486,402],{}," carries no zone at all and is only reachable by system participants.",[331,489,490,503],{},[334,491,492],{},[337,493,494,497,500],{},[340,495,496],{},"Participant",[340,498,499],{},"May send to",[340,501,502],{},"May subscribe to",[346,504,505,521,540],{},[337,506,507,510,518],{},[351,508,509],{},"APPLICATION (org, app)",[351,511,512,514,515],{},[288,513,435],{},", ",[288,516,517],{},"app.\u003Corg>.\u003Capp>",[351,519,520],{},"reply destinations only",[337,522,523,526,535],{},[351,524,525],{},"ORGANIZATION (org)",[351,527,528,514,530,514,532],{},[288,529,445],{},[288,531,435],{},[288,533,534],{},"app.\u003Corg>.*",[351,536,537,539],{},[288,538,534],{}," — its applications' zones",[337,541,542,545,548],{},[351,543,544],{},"SYSTEM",[351,546,547],{},"everything",[351,549,550],{},[288,551,455],{},[273,553,554],{},"Each server also has a zone partitioning, the zones it hosts and the zones it reaches. A node advertises a service\nto the cluster only in a zone its server hosts, and sends only to zones its server reaches: an address in any\nother zone has no handlers there. An address without a zone passes both.",[331,556,557,570],{},[334,558,559],{},[337,560,561,564,567],{},[340,562,563],{},"Server",[340,565,566],{},"Hosts",[340,568,569],{},"Reaches",[346,571,572,589,606],{},[337,573,574,577,581],{},[351,575,576],{},"org",[351,578,579],{},[288,580,445],{},[351,582,583,514,585,514,587],{},[288,584,445],{},[288,586,455],{},[288,588,435],{},[337,590,591,594,600],{},[351,592,593],{},"system",[351,595,596,514,598],{},[288,597,455],{},[288,599,445],{},[351,601,602,514,604],{},[288,603,455],{},[288,605,445],{},[337,607,608,610,617],{},[351,609,470],{},[351,611,612,514,614],{},[288,613,435],{},[288,615,616],{},"app.*",[351,618,619,514,621],{},[288,620,435],{},[288,622,616],{},[273,624,625],{},"The gateway applies the partitioning before a frame reaches the event bus: a send to a zone the server does not\nreach, or a subscription in a zone it does not host, is refused whatever the participant may address. The\nservice directory and listener monitors still see every registration in the cluster, so a service hosted by one\nserver shows as online from any other, while each server's MCP listing shows only the tools in zones it reaches.",[323,627,629],{"id":628},"resource-name","Resource Name",[273,631,632],{},"The name of the resource being addressed, excluding the zone. For services, this is the fully qualified service name. For streams, this is the event type name.",[281,634,637],{"className":635,"code":636,"language":286},[284],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService\nstream:\u002F\u002Fapp.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\n",[288,638,636],{"__ignoreMap":290},[323,640,642],{"id":641},"path","Path",[273,644,645],{},"An optional path that identifies a specific part of the resource, such as a method name on a service. The path's case is preserved.",[281,647,650],{"className":648,"code":649,"language":286},[284],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService\u002FfindById\nstream:\u002F\u002Fapp.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\u002Fsensor-1\n",[288,651,649],{"__ignoreMap":290},[323,653,655],{"id":654},"version","Version",[273,657,658],{},"An optional semantic version for the resource. Enables versioned service routing so multiple versions of a service can coexist.",[281,660,66